  @name "ACT5: Field of Crows"
  @first "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow"
  @sections "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain" "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast" "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell" "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses" "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners" "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries" "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law" "Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower" "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
__scene

section__
  @title "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-battlefront/frame-337.jpg"

  "Outside Highgarden, crushed thyme and wet straw cannot hide the groan of siege engines. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Sandor Clegane tests your posture in public while Gendry studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent. The promises you made in the war council are now being measured in bodies at the front.

Morale fractures are spreading faster than wounds heal. Units fight harder when they trust the next order will not waste them for politics.

You can distribute sacrifice transparently and risk slower action, or force outcomes through hidden pressure and keep momentum at the cost of trust. The next move will decide whether fear or discipline carries your front."

  choice__
    @target "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Confirm the plan by written oath, let rivals contest it publicly, and secure long-term trust over speed."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Run split instructions through deniable couriers, isolate rivals from their allies, and keep leverage off the books."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-battlefront/frame-338.jpg"

  "In Sunspear cells, heat, rust, and blood sit heavy while a prisoner bargains for one more breath. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Gendry tests your posture in public while Sandor Clegane studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent. Survivors from yesterday still carry those council promises like unpaid debt.

Tactical sacrifice is unavoidable now, but indiscriminate sacrifice becomes strategic suicide once soldiers believe survival depends on favoritism.

You can distribute sacrifice transparently and risk slower action, or force outcomes through hidden pressure and keep momentum at the cost of trust. The next move will decide whether fear or discipline carries your front."

  choice__
    @target "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Call captains into formal hearing, fix responsibility in record, and pay the time cost to restore legitimacy."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Make examples in shadow, leak only what serves your position, and lock compliance through controlled uncertainty."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-battlefront/frame-339.jpg"

  "At the Trident docks, brine and pitch smoke rise from chains bolted beside your treaty table. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Jaime Lannister tests your posture in public while Brienne of Tarth studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent.

You can hold ground with blood, but you cannot hold coalition confidence if casualty burdens look engineered instead of shared.

You can distribute sacrifice transparently and risk slower action, or force outcomes through hidden pressure and keep momentum at the cost of trust. The next move will decide whether fear or discipline carries your front."

  choice__
    @target "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Set one public standard for all houses, enforce it by decree, and accept short-term outrage for durable cohesion."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Turn hidden debts into blackmail leverage, compel cooperation without hearings, and preserve tempo at moral cost."
